'use strict';
/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Chapter 1 — Music theory.

   Everything about how music is put together, and nothing about microphones.
   Eleven lessons in four modules: Time, Pitch, Harmony, Melody. Each lesson is
   a list of blocks, and a block is one idea: a heading, a paragraph or two,
   then a picture of what was just said or a widget you can press.

   Rules this file keeps to, because breaking them is what made the old course
   feel like a series of jumps:
     · One new term per block, bolded where it is defined, never before.
     · No arithmetic in the first block of a lesson.
     · Nothing in the quiz that the body has not already explained.
     · Every figure shows the exact example the prose just described.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------- */

